  "$schema": "otterly tokens v2 — the single source of truth for constants/tokens.ts and build/tokens.css",
  "meta": {
    "version": "2.0",
    "date": "2026-11-01",
    "source": "Otterly Design Language v2 (Stage 2 of the November 2026 redesign), locked from Stage 1 Direction A 'Riverbank'. Supersedes tokens v1.2 (teal + coral, Fraunces / Nunito Sans / DM Mono).",
    "note": "v2.0 (1 Nov 2026). Palette: moss #244D3F is the voice, cream #F4EFE6 the ground, amber #E09F3E the one action (a fill only, always with ink text). Type: Newsreader for display AND figures (its default figures are tabular — verified: all ten digits share one advance width), Albert Sans for everything read (it has NO tabular figures, so it never sets a column of numbers). This file now lives IN THE APP REPO (build/tokens.json) — the design-folder copies had drifted behind constants/tokens.ts (they lacked map.dot, map.onPin and type.scale.figureStat), which is the exact failure the generator header warns about. Renamed roles keep their old names as deprecated aliases (see `aliases`) so nothing breaks before Stage 3/4 migrate the call sites; the generator writes each alias with its new value. Contrast-checked 1 Nov 2026: every text/background pair in both themes >= 4.5:1, control boundaries (inputBorder) >= 3:1; disabledText deliberately below (exempt). Panel round 1 Nov 2026 changed from Stage 1: dark band is a deep raised moss with cream text (not a pale reed slab); light textTertiary darkened #6B7770 -> #5C6862 to clear 4.5:1 on sunken; tab labels 12px Albert Sans 600 capped at 1.25x (Large Content Viewer beyond); secondary buttons are a tonal reed fill rather than a hairline outline. Stage 5 (1 Nov 2026): a switch's off track was 1.6:1 (light) and 1.4:1 (dark) against its surface, below the 3:1 a control's state needs; it now takes the inputBorder value in each theme (3.5:1 / 3.2:1), and the dark off knob is the text cream so it still stands off that track (3.5:1)."
  },
